{# Content slot: the Susi Q origin story (approved for web use, including her
   father, in CLIENT_FACTS.md), landing after the through-lines list. #}
{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>The senior work started at home. In 2010, my father came to live with me, and when I went looking for support for him, I found that most senior centers offered plenty to do, bingo, mahjong, a full social calendar, and almost nowhere to talk about what was actually hard. Someone could spend the whole day at a center and never once have space for the harder conversations.</p>
  <p>So I built one. It started as a group called Coffee Talk, later renamed Heart to Heart, and grew from there: Feeling the Blues for individuals over 55, a women's group, a men's group, a Death Cafe, a caregiver circle, a grief and loss group. People gravitate to real stories, and that is the truest one I have about how I work. I don't lead with technique. Techniques don't heal people. Relationships do.</p>
{% endcall %}
